<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Albert II, Prince of Monaco</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1958</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Albert II has been Sovereign Prince of Monaco since the death of his father Rainier III in 2005. A member of the Grimaldi family, he competed in bobsleigh at five Winter Olympics and is a member of the International Olympic Committee. His reign has emphasised environmental causes and Monaco's role as a financial and tourist centre, and in 2011 he married the South African swimmer Charlene <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wittstock">Wittstock</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/albert-ii-prince-of-monaco.jpg" alt="Albert II, Prince of Monaco" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lula Oficial · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Albert_II_-_08.06.2025_-_Encontro_com_Sua_Alteza_o_Pr%C3%ADncipe_de_M%C3%B4naco,_Alberto_II_(54574973880).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
